ee has a valid authenticated session and profile and vehicle records.","id":"AC-1.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned profile conforms to `EmployeeProfile`, identifies the authenticated employee, and includes the contract-defined employee fields, assigned parking status, assigned floor, and vehicles; an unauthenticated request has response status 401 and an authenticated identity without permission has response status 403.","when":"The employee requests `GET /me/profile`."},{"given":"An employee has a valid authenticated session and registered vehicles.","id":"AC-1.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned `vehicles` list conforms to `VehicleList` and contains only that employee's vehicles; a request without authentication has response status 401.","when":"The employee requests `GET /me/vehicles`."},{"given":"An employee has a valid authenticated session and submits a vehicle-registration request with a plate and optional vehicle details.","id":"AC-1.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned vehicle conforms to `Vehicle`, contains the submitted fields, and has status `Active`; invalid input has response status 400, missing authentication has response status 401, and a conflicting registration has response status 409, with each error response conforming to the contract `ApiError` schema.","when":"The employee sends the request to `POST /me/vehicles`."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":31,"lineStart":28,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"app.MapGet(\"/\", () => \"API is up\").ExcludeFromDescription();\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\napp.MapOpenApi();\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\"/openapi/v1.json\", \"API\"));"},{"lineEnd":15,"lineStart":8,"path":"contracts/openapi.yaml","quote":"security:\n  - oauth2:\n      - parking:access\npaths:\n  /auth/sessions:\n    post:\n      operationId: createSession\n      summary: Create a session from a Folio3 Google Workspace identity"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `POST /auth/sessions`, `GET /me/profile`, and `GET` and `POST /me/vehicles` with the request schemas, response schemas, security, and status behavior declared in the locked OpenAPI contract.","id":"REQ-1","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-1","I-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated employee requests the office configuration and the office has its contract-example initial configuration.","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response body conforms to `ParkingConfig`, with `officeTimezone` `Asia/Karachi`, `releaseTime` `08:00`, `schedulingWindowDays` 30, working days, and the holiday setting; a request without authentication has response status 401.","when":"The employee requests `GET /parking/config`."},{"given":"An employee has a valid authenticated session and parking data for the current office-local date.","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the response body conforms to `ParkingHome` and contains the office-local date and timezone, employee assignment and parking status, space status, release time, availability count, and contract-required vehicle and working-day fields; a request without authentication has response status 401.","when":"The employee requests `GET /parking/today`."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":31,"lineStart":28,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"app.MapGet(\"/\", () => \"API is up\").ExcludeFromDescription();\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\napp.MapOpenApi();\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\"/openapi/v1.json\", \"API\"));"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `GET /parking/config` and `GET /parking/today` using the configured office-local date and time and contract-defined response schemas; initial office configuration uses `Asia/Karachi`, release time `08:00`, and a 30-day scheduling window.","id":"REQ-2","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-1","ASM-7","ASM-8"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated dedicated parking holder has a reserved space today that has not already been released or claimed.","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned release identifies the office date, `Released` status, floor, space code, and `claimableAt`; before release time `claimableAt` is the configured office-local release time, and after release time it makes the space immediately available.","when":"The holder sends `POST /parking/releases/today` before or after the configured release time."},{"given":"A non-holder attempts a dedicated-holder release, or a holder attempts a release that conflicts with the current parking state.","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 for an ineligible employee or 409 for a conflicting state, and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema.","when":"The employee sends `POST /parking/releases/today`."},{"given":"An authenticated dedicated holder has saved releases and supplies optional `from` and `through` date filters where applicable.","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned releases list conforms to `ParkingReleaseList` and contains only matching saved releases in office-local dates; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-holder receives response status 403.","when":"The holder requests `GET /parking/releases`."},{"given":"An authenticated dedicated holder submits one or more valid dates within the configured scheduling window.","id":"AC-3.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned releases list contains one record for each accepted date with its release identifier, status, floor, space code, and `claimableAt` based on the configured office-local release time; invalid input has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, a non-holder receives response status 403, and a conflicting release has response status 409.","when":"The holder sends those dates to `POST /parking/releases`."},{"given":"An authenticated holder owns an existing unclaimed scheduled release.","id":"AC-3.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned release has status `Cancelled` and includes audit events for scheduling and cancellation; missing authentication has response status 401, a non-holder receives response status 403, an unknown identifier has response status 404, and a claimed or otherwise conflicting release has response status 409.","when":"The holder sends `DELETE /parking/releases/{releaseId}`."},{"given":"A dedicated holder submits a malformed date or a date outside the configured scheduling window.","id":"AC-3.6","level":"api","then":"The response status is the contract-declared 400 for invalid input or 409 for the applicable state conflict, and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema.","when":"The holder sends the date to `POST /parking/releases`."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":31,"lineStart":28,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"app.MapGet(\"/\", () => \"API is up\").ExcludeFromDescription();\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\napp.MapOpenApi();\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\"/openapi/v1.json\", \"API\"));"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `POST /parking/releases/today`, `GET` and `POST /parking/releases`, and `DELETE /parking/releases/{releaseId}` with contract-defined release eligibility, scheduling, filtering, cancellation, audit, and conflict behavior, calculated using the configured office-local timezone and release time.","id":"REQ-3","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-1","ASM-3","ASM-7","ASM-8"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated employee requests availability while released spaces are claimable.","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200, the response body conforms to `ParkingAvailability`, and its `availableSpaceCount` equals the number of records in its spaces list, each with the contract-defined identifier, floor, and code; a request without authentication has response status 401.","when":"The employee requests `GET /parking/availability`."},{"given":"An authenticated non-dedicated employee has a valid active registered vehicle and at least one claimable space.","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 201 and the returned claim conforms to `ParkingClaim` and identifies an active claim, allocated floor and space code, vehicle, authorized plate, entry status, floor capacities, and the contract allocation rule; invalid input has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, an ineligible employee receives response status 403, and a conflicting or unavailable allocation has response status 409.","when":"The employee sends the vehicle ID to `POST /parking/claims`."},{"given":"Two eligible employees request the last available space and one request is accepted first by the API.","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"The accepted response has status 201 and a returned active claim for the space, the other response has status 409, and the database contains exactly one active claim for that space.","when":"Both employees submit valid `POST /parking/claims` requests concurrently."},{"given":"An authenticated employee has a temporary claim for today, or has no temporary claim for today.","id":"AC-4.4","level":"api","then":"For a claim, the response status is 200 and the returned claim conforms to `ParkingClaim` and contains its assigned space, vehicle, authorized plate, and entry status; with no claim, the response status is 404 and the response error code is `not_found`; a request without authentication has response status 401.","when":"The employee requests `GET /parking/claims/today`."},{"given":"An authenticated employee requests cancellation of an existing active temporary claim.","id":"AC-4.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is 409 and the returned claim remains `Active`; missing authentication has response status 401, an identity without permission receives response status 403, and an unknown claim has response status 404.","when":"The employee sends `POST /parking/claims/{claimId}/cancel`."},{"given":"A dedicated holder requests a non-dedicated claim operation, or a non-dedicated employee requests a dedicated-holder release operation.","id":"AC-4.6","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema.","when":"The API receives the relevant claim or release request."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":31,"lineStart":28,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"app.MapGet(\"/\", () => \"API is up\").ExcludeFromDescription();\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\napp.MapOpenApi();\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\"/openapi/v1.json\", \"API\"));"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `GET /parking/availability`, `POST /parking/claims`, `GET /parking/claims/today`, and `POST /parking/claims/{claimId}/cancel` with contract-defined eligibility, allocation, concurrency, response, and cancellation behavior.","id":"REQ-4","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-1","ASM-3","ASM-7","ASM-8"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated parking administrator has employee roster records.","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned page conforms to `RosterPage`, contains matching employee records with contract-defined fields, and reports page and page-count fields; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.","when":"The administrator requests `GET /admin/roster` with optional search, assignment, page, and page-size parameters."},{"given":"An authenticated parking administrator has recorded entrance checks.","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned checks conform to `EntryCheckPage`, match the supplied filters, and contain the contract-defined verification date and time, plate, result, entry status, and detail; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.","when":"The administrator requests `GET /admin/entry-checks` with optional search, result, and page parameters."},{"given":"An authenticated parking administrator has retained parking activity.","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned events conform to `ActivityPage`, match the supplied filters and pagination, and contain the contract-defined office time, employee name, event, space or plate, and outcome; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.","when":"The administrator requests `GET /admin/activity` with optional search, event type, and page parameters."},{"given":"An authenticated standard employee requests an administrator-only list operation.","id":"AC-5.4","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.","when":"The employee requests any of the roster, entry-check, or activity list routes."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":31,"lineStart":28,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"app.MapGet(\"/\", () => \"API is up\").ExcludeFromDescription();\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\napp.MapOpenApi();\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\"/openapi/v1.json\", \"API\"));"}],"ears":"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator list operations `GET /admin/roster`, `GET /admin/entry-checks`, and `GET /admin/activity` with their contract-defined query filters, pagination, response schemas, and administrator authorization.","id":"REQ-5","op":"MODIFIED","sources":["I-1","ASM-3"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authenticated parking administrator requests a week for which parking and entrance records are available.","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned report conforms to `UtilizationReport` and contains the requested week dates, generation time, office timezone, released-space and temporary-claim counts, utilization percentage, daily statistics, and unused dedicated and temporary parking lists; an invalid date has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, and a non-administrator receives response status 403.","when":"The administrator requests `GET /admin/utilization` with an optional `weekStart`."},{"given":"A dedicated holder did not release a space and has no registered-vehicle entry record for a date, and a temporary claimant has no registered-vehicle entry record for a date.","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned report lists contain the corresponding `Unused Dedicated Parking` and `Unused Temporary Parking` events with employee, vehicle plate, and office-local date.","when":"An administrator requests the corresponding week through `GET /admin/utilization`."},{"given":"An authenticated standard employee requests a utilization report.","id":"AC-6.3","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.","when":"The employee requests `GET /admin/utilization`."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":31,"lineStart":28,"path":"App.Api/Program.cs","quote":"app.MapGet(\"/\", () => \"API is up\").ExcludeFromDescription();\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's 